toshaklg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toshaklg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toshaklg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toshaklg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toshaklg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toshaklg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T19:34:39Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T19:37:40Z","body":"I will comment as I have exactly the same issue with seemingly identical configuration: Windows 10 on Ryzen 5 5400H (with graphics) and GTX 1650. That is a laptop, if that's important.\n\nI also stumbled upon a fairly recent topic regarding Vulkan on AMD+NVIDIA configuration, and it seems that fiddling with environment variables solves the issue on Windows.\n\n\"Unable to launch Vulkan apps/game on notebooks with AMD Radeon iGPUs\": https://nvidia.custhelp.com/app/answers/detail/a_id/5182/~/unable-to-launch-vulkan-apps%2Fgame-on-notebooks-with-amd-radeon-igpus\n\nWith this set it is possible to create a project, but I have no clue about other possible effects.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749203536/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749308980","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103902#issuecomment-2749308980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103902","id":2749308980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j3yA0","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T20:24:06Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T20:24:06Z","body":"> I think the issue is while creating project only, later we can switch to forward+ and when we run our project it will show us the vulkan version.\n\nFor context, this is correct and \"expected\". The project manager defaults to an OpenGL context (more compatible, and faster to load), and has some logic to check whether RenderingDevice APIs are supported, to define whether users can make a Forward+ or Mobile project. In the past, we didn't check for this, and users were rightfully confused that right after creating a project, they can never open it successfully when their system doesn't support Vulkan.\n\nThe problem we found is that for some users with Nvidia drivers, this check for Vulkan support done from an OpenGL context triggers a crash. So we moved it to a separate process that only attempts to make a Vulkan context, and that seemed to solve the issue for affected users.\n\nNow this report shows that there's a third class of Nvidia users for whom even creating a Vulkan context in a separate process fails, yet running Godot directly with Vulkan seems to work.\n\nSo the workaround until we figure out why this happens, is to create projects with Compatibility, then change them to Forward+ or Mobile from the project settings.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749308980/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749309306","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103902#issuecomment-2749309306","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103902","id":2749309306,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j3yF6","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T20:24:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T20:24:16Z","body":"CC @bruvzg ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749309306/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749355460","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103902#issuecomment-2749355460","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103902","id":2749355460,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j39XE","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T20:46:44Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T20:46:44Z","body":"Vulkan init is the same in both cases, so this is strange. The only difference I see is disabling broken Vulkan layers, which is not done when running the test.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749355460/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749360662","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103902#issuecomment-2749360662","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103902","id":2749360662,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j3-oW","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T20:49:11Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T20:49:11Z","body":"> Vulkan init is the same in both cases, so this is strange. The only difference I see is disabling broken Vulkan layers, which is not done when running the test.\n\nThat might be the issue indeed, broken Vulkan layers can lead to Godot simply not being able to start.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749360662/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749483649","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103902#issuecomment-2749483649","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103902","id":2749483649,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j4cqB","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-24T21:51:41Z","updated_at":"2025-03-24T21:52:13Z","body":"> I also stumbled upon a fairly recent topic regarding Vulkan on AMD+NVIDIA configuration, and it seems that fiddling with environment variables solves the issue on Windows.\n\nThis is already done here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6b5b84c0c50135e88691e035d3e00c68a2ae5aa4/platform/windows/rendering_context_driver_vulkan_windows.cpp#L43-L48\n\nIt should no longer be required when using recent graphics drivers though.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749483649/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2749493292","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103902#issuecomment-2749493292","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103902","id":2749493292,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6j4fAs","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_u